{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:693c559e842aadf93ddcaba5f140c97aac1419c23fda3c1038c7a690c13b1213", "sample_idx": 34, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Section 1\nThe Guardian newspaper has issued corrections to several articles published on August 25th. These corrections address inaccuracies regarding details presented in various news stories and interviews. The corrections aim to ensure the accuracy and reliability of the information provided to readers. The newspaper is committed to upholding journalistic standards and promptly rectifying any errors that may occur. This demonstrates a dedication to transparency and accountability in their reporting.\n\n***\n\nSection 2\nOne correction clarifies the geographical scope of a new pet theft law. Initially reported as applying \"in the UK,\" the law actually applies specifically to England and Northern Ireland. Another correction concerns the description of Eileen Burbidge's role at Fertifa, stating she is the executive director, not the founder, with the founders being Tony Chen and Nick Kuan. Furthermore, a Q&A interview misidentified the director of a project as \"Lowther\" when the correct name is Lawther. \n\nSection 3\n* A previous article incorrectly identified the ethnicity of the family central to the film \"Bend It Like Beckham,\" stating they were Muslim when they are Sikh. \n*  Another error was made in reporting on Venetia Stanley's relationship with Herbert Asquith, where it was stated her father converted to Islam; the correction clarifies it was her uncle, the third Baron Stanley, who did so. The newspaper also noted other recently amended articles, including stories about Pavel Durov's arrest, royal servants, and the Salvator Mundi painting.\n\nSection 4\nReaders are invited to direct any further corrections or concerns to the Readers’ Editor via the provided address, email, or telephone number. This commitment to accuracy underscores the Guardian's dedication to providing reliable news coverage. The corrections highlight the importance of meticulous fact-checking in journalism and the need for ongoing vigilance in ensuring the information presented to the public is accurate and trustworthy.\n\nP.S. The corrections were made to various articles published on August 25th.\nP.P.S. The Reader's Editor contact information is provided for further inquiries.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Section", "logprob": -0.00034540885826572776}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.42889204621315}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -0.08256550878286362}, {"token": "▁Guardian", "logprob": -0.008356604725122452}, {"token": "▁newspaper", "logprob": -0.6573083400726318}, {"token": "▁has", "logprob": -0.025551341474056244}, {"token": "▁issued", "logprob": -0.0443553626537323}, {"token": "▁corrections", "logprob": -0.7257566452026367}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.00984928384423256}, {"token": "▁several", "logprob": -0.00015424491721205413}, {"token": "▁articles", "logprob": -0.045121174305677414}, {"token": "▁published", "logprob": -2.3007127310847864e-05}, {"token": "▁on", "logprob": -0.0006009918288327754}, {"token": "▁August", "logprob": -8.856858039507642e-05}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "2", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -3.4570634852570947e-06}, {"token": "th", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.009726985357701778}, {"token": "▁These", "logprob": -0.00893511064350605}, {"token": "▁corrections", "logprob": -0.13540171086788177}, {"token": "▁address", "logprob": -0.20422030985355377}, {"token": "▁inaccuracies", "logprob": -0.20731070637702942}, {"token": "▁regarding", "logprob": -1.3037114143371582}, {"token": "▁details", "logprob": -0.9403705596923828}, {"token": "▁presented", "logprob": -0.4575948417186737}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": -0.022275244817137718}, {"token": "▁various", "logprob": -0.6717337965965271}, {"token": 